fonts_trim_and_token_dedup.s:
Trim the Google Fonts payload (fewer families = faster LCP, less CLS from late font swaps) and collapse the duplicate font-token definitions between theme.css and variables.css.

Background facts, verified this session: fonts.css (line 1) imports 11 families. `Playfair Display` is DEAD — imported, referenced nowhere in src (grep for Playfair across src returns only fonts.css itself). `Montserrat` is used exactly once: +page.svelte:274, an SVG <text> in the home Journey diagram with `font-weight="700"` — but fonts.css loads only `Montserrat:ital,wght@0,900;1,500`, so 700 was ALREADY falling back to the system sans; the family has been decorative-broken since it was added. `Open Sans` is loaded as `wght@400` only, yet hero.css:87-91 (.welcome-text) sets `font-weight: 600` — the 600 is synthetic-bolds today. theme.css @theme lines 23-24 and 28 define `--font-display`, `--font-body`, `--font-welcome` AGAIN on :root (Tailwind v4 @theme emits them as :root custom properties), duplicating variables.css:34-39 and creating two sources of truth for the same property — and those three are NEVER used as Tailwind utility classes (grep for `font-display`/`font-body`/`font-welcome` classes returns zero). By contrast `--font-hero`, `--font-registration`, `--font-championship` (theme.css 25-27) ARE consumed as utilities (font-hero in ChampHero/PlatformCard/HomeJourney/+page.svelte; font-registration + font-championship in RegistrationForm.svelte) and MUST stay in @theme.

PHASE 1 — write the failing test first. Create src/styles/fonts.test.ts (new file, mirroring the readFileSync pattern of variables.test.ts):
```ts
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { resolve } from 'node:path';
import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';

const css = readFileSync(resolve(process.cwd(), 'src/styles/fonts.css'), 'utf8');

describe('fonts.css loaded families', () => {
  it('drops the unused Playfair Display and Montserrat families', () => {
    expect(css).not.toContain('Playfair');
    expect(css).not.toContain('Montserrat');
  });

  it('loads the 600 weight for Open Sans used by .welcome-text', () => {
    expect(css).toContain('Open+Sans:wght@400;600');
  });
});
```
Run `pnpm test` and confirm it fails: 'Playfair' and 'Montserrat' are both in the URL today, and Open Sans is `wght@400` not `400;600`. PHASE 2 = confirm the failure. PHASE 3 — implement:

A. src/styles/fonts.css line 1 — the single @import URL. Old (verbatim): `@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:wght@500&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Montserrat:ital,wght@0,900;1,500&family=Open+Sans:wght@400&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;1,500&family=Poppins:wght@700&family=Schibsted+Grotesk:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;1,500&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap');`
New (verbatim): `@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:wght@500&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Open+Sans:wght@400;600&family=Poppins:wght@700&family=Schibsted+Grotesk:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;1,500&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap');` (removed Montserrat + Playfair Display, widened Open Sans to 400;600).

B. src/routes/+page.svelte:274 — `font-family="'Montserrat', sans-serif"` → `font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif"` (Journey diagram AI chip: Space Grotesk is the loaded display face with a real 700 weight, so the chip finally renders in the intended font instead of a fallback).

C. src/styles/theme.css — delete lines 23, 24, and 28 (the `--font-display: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;`, `--font-body: 'Inter', sans-serif;`, `--font-welcome: 'Open Sans', sans-serif;` duplicates). Keep lines 25-27 (`--font-hero`, `--font-registration`, `--font-championship`). After the edit the @theme block reads:
```css
  --font-hero: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
  --font-registration: 'SN Pro', sans-serif;
  --font-championship: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
```
variables.css is now the single source for display/body/welcome; the removal cannot break the `font-hero`/`font-registration`/`font-championship` utilities because those tokens remain. Verify no `.font-display`/`.font-body`/`.font-welcome` class exists in src after the edit: `rg -n "font-(display|body|welcome)" src --glob '*.svelte'` must only match `var(--font-...)` usages, never `class="...font-display..."`.

PHASE 4 — fonts.test.ts green, variables.test.ts still green (it asserts no font strings), `pnpm test` + `pnpm check` pass. Why this exact trim: the two removed families were either dead (Playfair) or already-broken single-use (Montserrat 700 never loaded), so the LCP gain costs nothing visually; the Open Sans 600 load fixes a real synthetic-bold. This does not remove any @font-face block — SN Pro, GC Bumble, Fraunces local files stay (they are self-hosted, separate from the @import).
